From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 02:07:06 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 434/488] [DS4.1] Pair width as the selection's compile-time
 key; graph-safe cut reference

Run 17 timed select_first_argmax at 96 rows 0.05 us slower than Triton:
the pair width had become a runtime argument. It is a key again, and the
width-2 (Triton layout) kernel keeps its original key and code; the
runner's 16-byte pairs declare width 4.

The sink glue benchmark's torch cut reference set its start flags with a
CPU scalar, which graph capture refuses; it uses index_fill_.
---
 benchmarks/kernels/benchmark_sink_glue.py     |  2 +-
 .../v1/worker/gpu/sample/tilelang_sampling.py | 55 ++++++++++++-------
 .../worker/gpu/spec_decode/dspark/greedy.py   |  9 ++-
 3 files changed, 41 insertions(+), 25 deletions(-)

diff --git a/benchmarks/kernels/benchmark_sink_glue.py b/benchmarks/kernels/benchmark_sink_glue.py
index 2f9c5a856..1fe56204f 100644
--- a/benchmarks/kernels/benchmark_sink_glue.py
+++ b/benchmarks/kernels/benchmark_sink_glue.py
@@ -81,7 +81,7 @@ def torch_flags(columns, logits_indices, cu, num_reqs, dead_cut):
 def torch_cut(logits, flags, drafts, cu, num_reqs):
     num_logits, num_cols = logits.shape
     starts = torch.zeros(num_logits + 1, dtype=torch.bool, device=DEVICE)
-    starts[cu[:num_reqs].long()] = True
+    starts.index_fill_(0, cu[:num_reqs].long(), True)
     cols = drafts[1:num_logits].long()
     cut = flags[1:num_logits].bool() & ~starts[1:num_logits] & (cols >= 0)
     cut &= cols < num_cols
